{
  "title": "45: Al-Jathiyah الجاثية",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‌‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA MEEM.\nHa, Meem.\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(2)\nTANZEELUL KETAABE MENAL LAAHIL A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nThe [gradual] sending down of the Book is from Allah, the All-mighty, All-wise.\nاِنَّ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(3)\nINNA FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LA-AAYAATIL LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nIn the heavens and the earth there are indeed signs for the faithful,\nوَفِىْ خَلْقِكُمْ وَمَا يَبُثُّ مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ اٰيٰتٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nWA FEE KHALQEKUM WA MAA YABUSSO MIN DAABBATIN AAYAATUL LE-QAWMIN-Y YOOQENOON.\nThere are signs for people who have certainty in your own creation and in animals, He scatters abroad.\nوَاخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مِنْ رِّزْقٍ فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا وَ تَصْرِيْفِ الرِّيٰحِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWAKH TELAAFIL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE WA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO MENAS SAMAAA-E MIR RIZQIN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA WA TASREEFIR REYAAHE AAYAATUL LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’QELOON.\nThere are signs for people who exercise their reason in the alternation of night and day, in the provision that Allah sends down from the sky, with which He revives the earth after its death, and in the changing of the winds.\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ اللّٰهِ نَتْلُوْهَا عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ‌ۚ فَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَ اللّٰهِ وَاٰيٰتِهٖ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(6)\nTILKA AAYAATUL LAAHE NATLOOHAA A’LAYKA BIL-HAQ, FABE-AYYE HADEESIM BA’DAL LAAHE WA AAYAATEHI YOAMENOON.\nThese are the signs of Allah that We recite for you in truth. So what discourse will they believe after Allah and His signs?\nوَيْلٌ لِّكُلِّ اَفَّاكٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(7)\nWAYLUL LE-KULLE AFFAAKIN ASEEM.\nWoe to every sinful liar,\nيَّسْمَعُ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِ ثُمَّ يُصِرُّ مُسْتَكْبِرًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَسْمَعْهَا‌ ۚ فَبَشِّرْهُ بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(8)\nYASMA-O’ AAYAATIL LAAHE TUTLAA A’LAYHE SUMMA YOSIRRO MUSTAKBERAN KA-AL LAM YASMA’HAA, FA-BASH-SHIRHO BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nwho hears the signs of Allah being recited to him, yet persists arrogantly as if he had not heard them. So inform him of a painful punishment.\nوَاِذَا عَلِمَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا شَيْئًا اۨتَّخَذَهَا هُزُوًا‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ ؕ‏(9)\nWA EZAA A’LEMA MIN AAYAATENAA SHAY-ANIT TAKHAZAHAA HOZOWAA, OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUM MOHEEN.\nShould he learn anything about Our signs, he takes them in derision. For such there is a humiliating punishment.\nمِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ وَلَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَسَبُوْا شَيْئًا وَّلَا مَا اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌؕ‏(10)\nMINW WARAAA-EHIM JAHANNAM, WA LAA YUGHNEE A’NHUM MAA KASABOO SHAY-ANW WA LAA MAT TAKHAZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWLEYAAA, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nAhead of them is hell, and neither what they have earned, nor what they had taken as guardians besides Allah will avail them in any way, and there is a great punishment for them.\nهٰذَا هُدًى‌ ‌ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مِّنْ رِّجْزٍ اَلِيْمٌ‏(11)\nHAAZAA HODAA, WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATE RABBEHIM LAHUM A’ZAABUM MIR RIJZIN ALEEM.\nThis is [true] guidance, and there is a painful punishment due to defilement for those who defy the signs of their Lord.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ سَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْبَحْرَ لِتَجْرِىَ الْفُلْكُ فِيْهِ بِاَمْرِهٖ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nALLAAHUL LAZEE SAKH-KHARA LAKOMUL BAHRA LE-TAJREYAL FULKO FEEHE BE-AMREHI WA LE-TABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nIt is Allah who disposed the sea for you[r benefit] so that the ships may sail in it by His command, that you may seek of His bounty and that you may give thanks.\nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا مِّنْهُ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA SAKH-KHARA LAKUM MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’M MINH, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LE-QAWMIN-Y YATAFAKKAROON.\nHe has disposed for you[r benefit] whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth; all is from Him. There are indeed signs in that for a people who reflect.\nقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يَغْفِرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ اَيَّامَ اللّٰهِ لِيَجْزِىَ قَوْمًۢا بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(14)\nQUL LILLAZEENA AAMANOO YAGHFEROO LILLAZEENA LAA YARJOONA AYYAAMAL LAAHE LE-YAJZEYA QAWMAM BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nSay to the faithful to forgive those who do not expect Allah’s days, that He may [Himself] requite every people for what they used to earn.\nمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ اَسَآءَ فَعَلَيْهَا ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(15)\nMAN A’MELA SAALEHAN FALE-NAFSEH, WA MAN ASAAA-A FA-A’LAYHAA, SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM TURJA-O’ON.\nWhoever acts righteously, it is for his own soul, and whoever does evil, it is to its own detriment, then you will be brought back to your Lord.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAL KETAABA WAL HUKMA WAN NOBUWWATA WA RAZAQNAAHUM MENAT TAYYEBAATE WA FAZZALNAAHUM A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nCertainly We gave the Children of Israel the Book, judgement and prophethood and We provided them with all the good things. We gave them an advantage over all the nations,\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ بَيِّنٰتٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ‌ ۚ فَمَا اخْتَلَفُوْۤا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ ۙ بَغْيًاۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(17)\nWA AATAYNAAHUM BAYYENAATIM MENAL AMR, FAMAKH TALAFOO ILLAA MIM BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL I’LMO, BAGHYAM BAYNAHUM, INNA RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM YAWMAL QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nand We gave them manifest precepts. But they did not differ except after knowledge had come to them, out of envy among themselves. Indeed your Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning that about which they used to differ.\nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰكَ عَلٰى شَرِيْعَةٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ فَاتَّبِعْهَا وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(18)\nSUMMA JA-A’LNAAKA A’LAA SHAREE-A’TIM MENAL AMRE FAT-TABE’HAA WA LAA TATTABE’ AHWAAA-AL LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThen We set you upon a clear course of the Law; so follow it, and do not follow the desires of those who do not know.\nاِنَّهُمْ لَنْ يُّغْنُوْا عَنْكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍ‌ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ وَلِىُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(19)\nINNAHUM LAN-Y YUGHNOO A’NKA MENAL LAAHE SHAY-AA, WA INNAZ ZAALEMEENA BA’ZOHUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z, WAL LAAHO WALIYYUL MUTTAQEEN.\nIndeed they will not avail you in any way against Allah. Indeed the wrongdoers are allies of one another, but Allah is the ally of the Godwary.\nهٰذَا بَصَائِرُ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَ‏(20)\nHAAZAA BASAAA-ERO LIN-NAASE WA HODANW WA RAHMATUL LE-QAWMIN-Y YOOQENOON.\nThese are eye-openers for mankind, and guidance and mercy for a people who have certainty.\nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ اجْتَرَحُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ نَّجْعَلَهُمْ كَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ۙ سَوَآءً مَّحْيَاهُمْ وَمَمَاتُهُمْ‌ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(21)\nAM HASEBAL LAZEENAJ TARAHUS SAYYE-AATE AN NAJ-A’LAHUM KALLAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE, SAWAAA-AM MAHYAAHUM WA MAMAATOHUM, SAAA-A MAA YAHKOMOON.\nDo those who have perpetrated misdeeds suppose that We shall treat them like those who have faith and do righteous deeds, their life and death being equal? Evil is the judgement that they make!\nوَ خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ وَلِتُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA KHALAQAL LAAHUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQQE WA LE-TUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT WA HUM LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAllah created the heavens and the earth with consummate wisdom, so that every soul may be requited for what it has earned, and they will not be wronged.\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰهَهٗ هَوٰٮهُ وَاَضَلَّهُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ وَّخَتَمَ عَلٰى سَمْعِهٖ وَقَلْبِهٖ وَجَعَلَ عَلٰى بَصَرِهٖ غِشٰوَةً  ؕ فَمَنْ يَّهْدِيْهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(23)\nAFA-RA-AYTA MANIT TAKHAZA ELAAHAHU HAWAAHO WA AZALLAHUL LAAHO A’LAA I’LMINW WA KHATAMA A’LAA SAM-E’HI WA QALBEHI WA JA-A’LA A’LAA BASAREHI GHESHAAWAH, FAMAN-Y YAHDEEHE MIM BA’DIL LAAH, AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nHave you seen him who has taken his desire to be his god and whom Allah has led astray knowingly, set a seal upon his hearing and heart, and put a blindfold on his sight? So who will guide him after Allah [has consigned him to error]? Will you not then take admonition?\nوَقَالُوْا مَا هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوْتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا يُهْلِكُنَاۤ اِلَّا الدَّهْرُ‌ؕ وَمَا لَهُمْ بِذٰلِكَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ ۚ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَظُنُّوْنَ‏(24)\nWA QAALOO MAA HEYA ILLAA HAYAATONAD DUNYAA NAMOOTO WA NAHYAA WA MAA YOHLEKONAA ILLAD DAHR, WA MAA LAHUM BEZAALEKA MIN I’LM, IN HUM ILLAA YAZUNNOON.\nThey say, ‘There is nothing but the life of this world: we live and we die, and nothing but time destroys us.’ But they do not have any knowledge of that, and they only make conjectures.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ مَّا كَانَ حُجَّتَهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا ائْتُوْا بِاٰبَآئِنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAATIM MAA KAANA HUJJATAHUM ILLAA AN QAALOATOO BE-AABAAA-ENAA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nWhen Our manifest signs are recited to them, their only argument is to say, ‘Bring our fathers back [to life], if you are truthful.’\nقُلِ اللّٰهُ يُحْيِيْكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيْتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يَجْمَعُكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(26)\nQOLIL LAAHO YOHYEEKUM SUMMA YOMEETOKUM SUMMA YAJMA-O’KUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEHE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSay, ‘It is Allah who gives you life, then He makes you die. Then He will gather you on the Day of Resurrection, in which there is no doubt. But most people do not know.’\nوَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَيَوْمَ تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّخْسَرُ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(27)\nWA LILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WA YAWMA TAQOOMUS SAA-A’TO YAWMA-EZIN-Y YAKHSARUL MUBTELOON.\nTo Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and when the Hour sets in, the falsifiers will be losers on that day.\nوَتَرٰى كُلَّ اُمَّةٍ جَاثِيَةً‌ كُلُّ اُمَّةٍ تُدْعٰۤى اِلٰى كِتٰبِهَا ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA TARAA KULLA UMMATIN JAASEYAH, KULLO UMMATIN TUD-A’A ELAA KETAABEHAA, AL-YAWMA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd you will see every nation fallen on its knees. Every nation will be summoned to its book: ‘Today you will be requited for what you used to do.\nهٰذَا كِتٰبُنَا يَنْطِقُ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ اِنَّا كُنَّا نَسْتَنْسِخُ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nHAAZAA KETAABONAA YANTEQO A’LAYKUM BIL-HAQ, INNAA KUNNAA NASTANSEKHO MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThis is Our book, which speaks truly against you. Indeed We used to record what you used to do.’\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَيُدْخِلُهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(30)\nFA-AMMAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FA-YUDKHELOHUM RABBOHUM FEE RAHMATEH, ZAALEKA HOWAL FAWZUL MOBEEN.\nAs for those who have faith and do righteous deeds, their Lord will admit them into His mercy. That is the manifest success!\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَفَلَمْ تَكُنْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَاسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ وَكُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA AMMAL LAZEENA KAFAROO, AFALAM TAKUN AAYAATEE TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FASTAKBARTUM WA KUNTUM QAWMAM MUJREMEEN.\nBut as for the faithless, [they will be asked,] ‘Were not My signs recited to you? But you were disdainful, and you were a guilty lot.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّالسَّاعَةُ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا قُلْتُمْ مَّا نَدْرِىْ مَا السَّاعَةُ ۙ اِنْ نَّظُنُّ اِلَّا ظَنًّا وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِمُسْتَيْقِنِيْنَ‏(32)\nWA EZAA QEELA INNA WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUNW WAS SAA-A’TO LAA RAYBA FEEHAA QULTUM MAA NADREE MAS SAA-A’TO, IN NAZUNNO ILLAA ZANNANW WA MAA NAHNO BE-MUSTAYQENEEN.\nWhen it was said, ‘‘Allah’s promise is indeed true, and there is no doubt about the Hour,’’ you said, ‘‘We do not know what the Hour is. We know nothing beyond conjectures, and we do not possess any certainty.’’ ’\nوَبَدَا لَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA BADAA LAHUM SAYYE-AATO MAA A’MELOO WA HAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZE-OON.\nThe evils of what they had done will appear to them, and they will be besieged by what they used to deride.\nوَقِيْلَ الْيَوْمَ نَنْسٰٮكُمْ كَمَا نَسِيْتُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا وَمَاْوٰٮكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA QEELAL YAWMA NANSAAKUM KAMAA NASEETUM LEQAAA-A YAWMEKUM HAAZAA WA MAAWAAKOMUN NAARO WA MAA LAKUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nAnd it will be said, ‘Today We will forget you, just as you forgot the encounter of this day of yours. The Fire will be your abode, and you will not have any helpers.\nذٰلِكُمْ بِاَنَّكُمُ اتَّخَذْتُمْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ هُزُوًا وَّغَرَّتْكُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ فَالْيَوْمَ لَا يُخْرَجُوْنَ مِنْهَا وَلَا هُمْ يُسْتَعْتَبُوْنَ‏(35)\nZAALEKUM BE-ANNAKOMUT TAKHAZTUM AAYAATIL LAAHE HOZOWANW WA GHARRATKOMUL HAYAATUD DUNYAA, FALYAWMA LAA YUKHRAJOONA MINHAA WA LAA HUM YUSTA’TABOON.\nThat is because you took the signs of Allah in derision, and the life of the world had deceived you.’ So today, they will not be brought out of it, nor will they be asked to propitiate [Allah].\nفَلِلّٰهِ الْحَمْدُ رَبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَرَبِّ الْاَرْضِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(36)\nFALILLAAHIL HAMDO RABBIS SAMAAWAATE WA RABBIL ARZE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSo all praise belongs to Allah, the Lord of the heavens and the Lord of the earth, the Lord of all the worlds.\nوَلَهُ الْكِبْرِيَآءُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(37)\nWA LAHUL KIBREYAAA-O FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nTo Him belongs all supremacy in the heavens and the earth, and He is the All-mighty, the All-wise.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Jaaseyah (The Kneeling)\nThere are 37 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. This Surah is also called Surah al-Shari’ah. It is narrated that whoever recites this Surah will not be frightened on the Day of Judgement and his private parts will remain covered (whereas all people will be raised naked on this day).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah will not see Jahannam and neither will he hear the voice of its flames. Keeping this Surah in one’s possession makes him a beloved of the people and protects him from tyrant rulers. It also keeps one safe from those who love to slander and backbite. If it is placed on the neck of a newborn child, it ensures safety and protection from all calamities."
}
